Q: Converting non-constant wide character strings to multibyte character strings, C not C++ A: <p>Use a cast.</p>
<pre><code>wcsrtombs(result, (const wchar_t**)&amp;buffer, len, &amp;ps);
</code></pre>
<p>If casts are frowned upon in your environment, use an intermediate variable.</p>
<pre><code>const wchar_t* constBuffer = buffer;
wcsrtombs(result, &amp;constBuffer, len, &amp;ps);
</code></pre>
